  "slug": "spatial-transcriptomics-6c8f",
  "summary": "Repeated sampling of living tissue and joint accessibility-isoform profiling extend spatial and single-cell transcriptomics beyond static snapshots.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is adding temporal or isoform-level resolution to transcriptomics. LIFE-seq (nanoforest arrays) and LANCE-seq (encoded microneedle arrays) sample living tissue repeatedly; LIFE-seq follows cortical injury within the same mouse, and LANCE-seq profiles mouse brain and tracks APAP-induced liver injury over time. FULL-seq jointly profiles chromatin accessibility and full-length transcripts per cell, linking promoter regulation to alternative first exon usage. SpaceMACE adds spatial proximity and expression similarity to tumour-cell annotation, and PDAC BioPortal integrates bulk, single-nucleus and spatial cohorts. The remaining items apply transcriptomic profiling to cervical tissue and cancer or examine KDM3B-driven ErbB signaling in cholangiocarcinoma, and they do not emphasize temporal or isoform resolution.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
